## Advance, revisit, pause, and escalate

Advance after teach commits two distinct qualifying full passes; initial acquisition and delayed retention remain separate observations. After one failure, score, explain the named repair and use another unused item. After two unsuccessful independent attempts, pause repeated quizzing and revisit the explanation or diagnostic dependency. Source conflict stops the affected lesson and goes to ingest with the exact note heading. Missing or ambiguous keys, unsupported alternatives and an exhausted bank go to plan as plan_issue with 2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal, O011, revision2/O011-C1, P004/V003/ingestion3 and the exact item ID. Closing a partial session does not fabricate acquisition.

## Answer-free recall handoff

Topic: Separate corrective taxation, revenue use and double-dividend claims. Instruction: Begin a closed-note review with teach for O011; request an unused prepared delayed item before recap. Lesson: [[03_Agents/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal/lessons/O011.md#Immediate and delayed checks]]. Teach supplies committed evidence and timestamps; recall alone assigns due dates or Todoist tasks. Deadline/retention horizon is null; this plan defines no learner result.

## Content provenance and generation boundaries

Complete checked-note passages above are reused with only heading-depth and explicit mathematical typography adaptation; exact origin/fingerprint and asset dependencies are in source_manifest.md. All earlier plan-created exercises/full keys and named evidence routes remain intact. Hypothetical arithmetic instantiates the included definitions and does not introduce empirical results or new academic claims. Only named prepared full-capability forms and their existing permitted pairs can certify acquisition/delayed evidence. Extra checked explanation/practice cannot replace a named full form or reassessment gate. Equivalent verified methods may meet the unchanged pre-answer criterion; ambiguous criteria or an exhausted fresh bank return to plan. The current objective revision is 2; item/criterion versions remain as explicitly stated above.
